% Exact, sargable, and guarded column bindings for index acceleration.

### name: bind.exact.mariadb
--- note
exact: true skips CAST(... AS CHAR) and COLLATE utf8mb4_bin, restoring index usage.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
(`cms_entry`.`typepath` = 'home')
===

### name: bind.exact.sqlite
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
("cms_entry"."typepath" = 'home')
===

### name: bind.exact.postgresql
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
("cms_entry"."typepath" = 'home')
===

### name: bind.exact.two-columns
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "column": "a", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "B": {"kind": "column", "column": "b", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
A $== B
--- expect
(`a` = `b`)
===

### name: bind.exact.ordering
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "column": "a", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
A $< "z"
--- expect
(`a` < 'z')
===

### name: bind.sargable.mariadb
--- note
sargable: true generates a coarse equality prefilter to leverage indexes on _ci columns,
followed by the exact binary collation check as residual.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
((`cms_entry`.`typepath` = 'home') AND (CAST(`cms_entry`.`typepath` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('home' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin))
===

### name: bind.sargable.postgresql
--- note
On PostgreSQL text equality is already exact, so sargable emits clean bare equality.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
("cms_entry"."typepath" = 'home')
===

### name: bind.sargable.sqlite
--- note
On SQLite text equality is already exact, so sargable emits clean bare equality.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
("cms_entry"."typepath" = 'home')
===

### name: bind.in.exact.mariadb
--- note
exact: true causes IN expansion over literal list to emit bare equality comparisons,
allowing B-tree index range scans.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"STATUS": {"kind": "column", "column": "status", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
STATUS IN ("open", "held")
--- expect
((`status` = 'open') OR (`status` = 'held'))
===

### name: bind.in.exact.postgresql
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"STATUS": {"kind": "column", "column": "status", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
STATUS IN ("open", "held")
--- expect
(("status" = 'open') OR ("status" = 'held'))
===

### name: bind.in.exact.sqlite
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"STATUS": {"kind": "column", "column": "status", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}}
--- source
STATUS IN ("open", "held")
--- expect
(("status" = 'open') OR ("status" = 'held'))
===

### name: bind.guard.mariadb
--- note
guard: true forces numeric guard checks even when the column binding is declared NUM.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"VAL": {"kind": "column", "column": "val", "type": "NUM", "guard": true}}
--- source
VAL == 25
--- expect
(CASE WHEN (`val` REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(`val` AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END = 25)
===

### name: bind.guard.postgresql
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"VAL": {"kind": "column", "column": "val", "type": "NUM", "guard": true}}
--- source
VAL == 25
--- expect
(CASE WHEN (CAST("val" AS TEXT) ~ '^-?[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$') THEN CAST("val" AS NUMERIC) ELSE NULL END = 25)
===

### name: bind.guard.sqlite-refusal
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"VAL": {"kind": "column", "column": "val", "type": "NUM", "guard": true}}
--- source
VAL == 25
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===

### name: bind.collation.binary
--- note
Aliases collation="binary" to exact=true.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "collation": "binary"}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
(`cms_entry`.`typepath` = 'home')
===

### name: bind.collation.sargable
--- note
Aliases collation="sargable" to sargable=true.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "collation": "sargable"}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
((`cms_entry`.`typepath` = 'home') AND (CAST(`cms_entry`.`typepath` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('home' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin))
===

### name: bind.sargable.derived-dialect
--- note
A derived dialect extending MariaDB inherits sargablePrefilter from mysql-family.
--- dialect
cms-mariadb
--- register
[{"dialect": "cms-mariadb", "extends": "mariadb", "version": "11.8"}]
--- bindings
{"TYPEPATH": {"kind": "column", "table": "cms_entry", "column": "typepath", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}
--- source
TYPEPATH $== "home"
--- expect
((`cms_entry`.`typepath` = 'home') AND (CAST(`cms_entry`.`typepath` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('home' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin))
===

### name: bind.separate.relation.mariadb
--- note
prefilter: "separate" on relation emits two sibling EXISTS subqueries conjoined by AND on MariaDB.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"FIELDS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "cms_fields", "alias": "g", "correlate": {"raw": "`g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid`"}, "prefilter": "separate", "fields": {"fname": {"table": "g", "column": "fname", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "value": {"table": "g", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}}}
--- source
ANY(FIELDS, G, G["fname"] $== "f_group" AND G["value"] $== "news")
--- expect
(EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND (`g`.`value` = 'news'))) IS TRUE) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND ((`g`.`value` = 'news') AND (CAST(`g`.`value` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('news' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)))) IS TRUE))
===

### name: bind.separate.column.mariadb
--- note
prefilter: "separate" on column propagates through ANY when relation leaves prefilter unspecified.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"FIELDS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "cms_fields", "alias": "g", "correlate": {"raw": "`g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid`"}, "fields": {"fname": {"table": "g", "column": "fname", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "value": {"table": "g", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true, "prefilter": "separate"}}}}
--- source
ANY(FIELDS, G, G["fname"] $== "f_group" AND G["value"] $== "news")
--- expect
(EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND (`g`.`value` = 'news'))) IS TRUE) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND ((`g`.`value` = 'news') AND (CAST(`g`.`value` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('news' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)))) IS TRUE))
===

### name: bind.separate.splitsargable.mariadb
--- note
splitSargable: true alias on relation is treated as prefilter: "separate".
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"FIELDS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "cms_fields", "alias": "g", "correlate": {"raw": "`g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid`"}, "splitSargable": true, "fields": {"fname": {"table": "g", "column": "fname", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "value": {"table": "g", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}}}
--- source
ANY(FIELDS, G, G["fname"] $== "f_group" AND G["value"] $== "news")
--- expect
(EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND (`g`.`value` = 'news'))) IS TRUE) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND ((`g`.`value` = 'news') AND (CAST(`g`.`value` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('news' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)))) IS TRUE))
===

### name: bind.separate.inline-override.mariadb
--- note
Relation prefilter: "inline" overrides column-level prefilter: "separate".
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"FIELDS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "cms_fields", "alias": "g", "correlate": {"raw": "`g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid`"}, "prefilter": "inline", "fields": {"fname": {"table": "g", "column": "fname", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "value": {"table": "g", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true, "prefilter": "separate"}}}}
--- source
ANY(FIELDS, G, G["fname"] $== "f_group" AND G["value"] $== "news")
--- expect
EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `cms_fields` `g` WHERE `g`.`cmsid` = `cms_entry`.`cmsid` AND (((`g`.`fname` = 'f_group') AND ((`g`.`value` = 'news') AND (CAST(`g`.`value` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('news' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)))) IS TRUE)
===

### name: bind.separate.postgresql
--- note
On PostgreSQL sargable equality does not create a separate coarse prefilter, emitting a single clean EXISTS subquery.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"FIELDS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "cms_fields", "alias": "g", "correlate": {"raw": "\"g\".\"cmsid\" = \"cms_entry\".\"cmsid\""}, "prefilter": "separate", "fields": {"fname": {"table": "g", "column": "fname", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "value": {"table": "g", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}}}
--- source
ANY(FIELDS, G, G["fname"] $== "f_group" AND G["value"] $== "news")
--- expect
EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM "cms_fields" "g" WHERE "g"."cmsid" = "cms_entry"."cmsid" AND ((("g"."fname" = 'f_group') AND ("g"."value" = 'news'))) IS TRUE)
===

### name: bind.separate.sqlite
--- note
On SQLite sargable equality does not create a separate coarse prefilter, emitting a single clean EXISTS subquery.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"FIELDS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "cms_fields", "alias": "g", "correlate": {"raw": "\"g\".\"cmsid\" = \"cms_entry\".\"cmsid\""}, "prefilter": "separate", "fields": {"fname": {"table": "g", "column": "fname", "type": "TEXT", "exact": true}, "value": {"table": "g", "column": "value", "type": "TEXT", "sargable": true}}}}
--- source
ANY(FIELDS, G, G["fname"] $== "f_group" AND G["value"] $== "news")
--- expect
EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM "cms_fields" "g" WHERE "g"."cmsid" = "cms_entry"."cmsid" AND ((("g"."fname" = 'f_group') AND ("g"."value" = 'news'))) IS TRUE)
===

